{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["Shelamim — since it is not the expression of burnt-offering, it is not entirely consumed, but rather the expression of shelamim. It conveys the sense of a vow, and one must fulfill his vows — which is the language of payment — and then its ruling is as I proceed to explain. Our Rabbis explained: the expression of shalom, for everyone has a share in it: its portions to the One on high, breast and thigh to the priests, its flesh eaten by the owners."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:12.294536021Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}